// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// App-wide settings that aren't tied to any single note/todo — the
// counterpart to entry-note.mdix/entry-todo.mdix's per-entry
// headerTheme/bodyTheme fields. Right now this only documents those two
// (the landing/list page's own default backgrounds, set from the
// Settings sheet — see settings.svelte.ts's appHeaderTheme/
// appBodyTheme). It deliberately does NOT also retrofit a schema for
// fontSize/debugPanelVisible/noteLinesEnabled: those already lived in
// settings.svelte.ts as plain localStorage values with no .mdix mirror
// before this file existed, and folding them in wasn't part of what
// this pass covered — doing that unasked would be guessing at a schema
// for fields nobody's confirmed need one yet. This file exists because
// the landing-page theme specifically needed a real DixScript home (it
// reuses Themes.theme_preset()/theme_custom() from themes.mdix, same
// pointer shape as an entry's own theme), not as a claim that app
// settings as a whole are DixScript-backed now — they aren't;
// storage.ts/settings.svelte.ts are still the TEMPORARY localStorage
// layer, same as everything else pending src-tauri/src/data/entries.rs.
//
// REVISION: was a single `theme` field, applied identically to both the
// top app-bar AND the scrollable list behind it — split into
// appHeaderTheme (AppHeader.svelte's own <header> specifically —
// confirmed against an annotated screenshot) and appBodyTheme
// (everything else, including the Notes/Todos tab row, which turned out
// to actually be part of "body" and not "header" — see
// AppHeader.svelte/+page.svelte's own comments on this same
// correction). No icon field here — see entry-note.mdix's icon comment:
// an icon is pinned to one specific note/todo, there's no landing-page
// equivalent.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "Mid-D-Man"
  features   -> "data,imports,quickfuncs"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@IMPORTS(
  Themes from "themes.mdix"
)

@DATA(
  appHeaderTheme = Themes.theme_preset("none")
  appBodyTheme   = Themes.theme_preset("none")
)
